# Local env, never commit real credentials. .env.example is the template.
# The wildcards matter: a stray .env.backup or .env.old holds live keys
# just as surely as .env does.
#
# ORDER MATTERS HERE. A later .env* pattern used to sit at the bottom of
# this file and quietly re-ignored the template, so .env.example was never
# committed and nobody could see which variables a deployment needs. The
# negation has to come last.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
